    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2024/10/saucony-tempus-2-review-2024.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The dual-foam setup feels moderately firm rather than plush, with softer rearfoot compression for impact protection; heel landings are mostly smooth after break-in, while the forefoot feels stiffer with limited flex.",
        "Responsiveness: The midsole is snappy with noticeable bounce (especially at steady-to-fast paces) and can respond to tempo changes, but it can feel slightly mushy/slow when trying to change gears at higher uptempo efforts.",
        "Stability: Stability is a core strength, with a supportive frame, very stiff/non-flexible midfoot (high torsional rigidity), secure lockdown, and a thick/stiff heel counter that improves control but may feel intrusive for sensitive heels.",
        "Durability: Overall durability is rated above average, but outsole/grip performance is a weakness on wet smooth surfaces due exposed foam and limited traction."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2024/11/saucony-tempus-2-review.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The ride is notably soft and protective for tired legs, with a firmer heel feel from PWRRUN EVA and a softer/more forgiving forefoot-center feel from PWRRUN PB.",
        "Responsiveness: It has solid energy return and enough bounce for strides/faster paces, but feels less springy and less snappy than plated Endorphin options.",
        "Stability: Stability is strong but unobtrusive; a wide platform, medial sidewalls, and guidance-frame geometry provide dependable lateral support while keeping a fairly neutral underfoot feel.",
        "Durability: The XT-900 carbon-rubber outsole delivered good grip across wet pavement/gravel/dirt and showed no meaningful wear at roughly 60 miles, indicating good durability."
      ]
    }
